  "review_note": "Boss1 adopts three fully checked current deliveries and four fully reviewed peer packets: RET21, ROOT-TAX19, SECURITY2, Cheng-Mao original 3A, shared-cycle policy proof application, seven-maxima private-deficit bridge, and Santa unknown-threshold clock 3C. Root performed substantive mathematical reconstruction and original source comparisons, with independent worker reviews where specified. Exact current receipts, input versions and evidence are frozen. Inherited mature proof/audit scopes remain explicitly distinguished from newly read material; no scientific algorithms or LP were rerun. Replacement relations retain their stable IDs and supersession dispositions; no unrelated pending comparison is discharged.",
  "archive_notes": {
    "archives/customer-attraction": {
      "comparison_scope": "Current RET21 and ROOT-TAX19 source repairs, all current SECURITY2 coverage, exact same complete-policy sources for shared-cycle four saved policies, and the seven-maxima fixed-route size halfspace against the true six-provider optimal union. Root reviewed all new relations, supersession dispositions and target scopes, not just endpoint names.",
      "outcome": "Uniform retained fixed root comparison pools imply the static private-block loss inequality, while conditional pool restart has its own explicit identity and cannot silently replace the root pool. Existing all-prefix CA family refutes the cumulative RET payment premise; the half bridge using that premise remains an explicitly blocked conditional route. Root-tax AAAF inequalities refer to static total profit, not RET coverage, and its local private-floor/square-credit specializations remain exact. Common-Q averaging for selected fixed policies is finite context and does not prove general query/total-payoff equivalence. Shared-cycle source proof certifies all-history IC and exact W/OPT for four actual functions, with contribution scope preserving unproved cone optimality and other computations. Fixed-policy IC proof application is not equality of the source and target strategies. Seven-maxima contribution combines the rational fixed-route halfspace certificate with OPT6=Nplus-min private block; the missing (p1-min p)/2 charge is explicit and not deleted by relabeling."
    },
    "archives/customer-attraction/subarchives/six-providers": {
      "comparison_scope": "Joint use of the exact 000010 size-halfspace margin and seven-maxima private-block optimal-objective identity for the exact-six full-history half target.",
      "outcome": "The single ALL contribution proves W-OPT6/2 >= delta*Nplus-(p1-min p)/2. The explicit additional small-deficit condition pays half on that branch. Unused-label normalization keeps 0 and 1 fixed, and the size condition does not remove the private deficit. Remaining routes, size complement, large deficit and other maximal-catalog counts are preserved; no whole general-six claim is made."
    },
    "archives/unrelated-machines": {
      "comparison_scope": "Complete Cheng-Mao 99/26 construction/duality/finite signature review versus the 4+delta algorithm, followed by its arbitrary feasible positive threshold interface and the exact total-bit-clock requirement needed for historical GA-05.",
      "outcome": "The 26/99 guarantee pays 4+delta numerical existence only, not the efficient target algorithm. All-config thin cases, half charging, dummy strictness and finite signatures were reviewed with honest fresh-versus-inherited PDF scope. A specified uniform polynomial total bit clock for one fixed Appendix C implementation suffices to compile an unknown-optimum algorithm by rational scaling, truncation and actual allocation validation. The 4+delta state geometry and positive parameters do not supply this clock."
    },
    "archives/bottleneck-knapsack": {
      "comparison_scope": "GA-05 exact historical restricted Santa Claus algorithm contract versus Cheng-Mao Appendix C through the new fully reviewed 3C clock bridge.",
      "outcome": "Under the explicit open uniform clock P, integer threshold search maintains only hi>Tstar and a verified allocation at lambda*lo; success need not be monotone or prove LP feasibility. This yields a total bit-polynomial actual allocation with fixed delta=5/26, preserving resources, eligibility, all players and zero-target cases. The conditional whole_result is complete; P and GA-05 historical status are unchanged. Finite termination and the other 4+delta algorithm do not turn this into an unconditional break-four result."
    }
  },
  "cross_archive_scope": "One substantive cross-archive bridge is adopted: the actual restricted Santa Claus construction in unrelated-machines to historical GA-05 in bottleneck-knapsack, with the uniform total-bit-clock condition and unknown-threshold compilation proved explicitly. Customer-attraction relations were independently reviewed in their own model.",
  "cross_archive_outcome": "The Santa bridge is accepted conditional whole_result; the original numerical existence edge remains unconditional contribution. No customer-attraction-to-Santa relation is inferred from common integration. Unreviewed concurrent changes and exact open mathematical obligations remain pending."
}
